// Blinder Tunnel - ShelbyLoader V2 "MicrosoftRuntime" Run-Key Persistence
// Rationale:   ShelbyLoader V2 (RuntimeBroker.dll, Unit 42 and Nextron variants) re-asserts
//              HKCU\...\Run\MicrosoftRuntime on a 120s then hourly timer, pointing at a quoted
//              %LOCALAPPDATA%\Microsoft\RuntimeBrokers\RuntimeBroker.exe. The genuine RuntimeBroker.exe
//              is a System32 COM broker that is never autostarted from a Run key, so either the
//              implant's value name or the binary name in Run data is a near-binary signal that
//              needs no allow-list.
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1547.001 - Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder
//               T1036.005 - Masquerading: Match Legitimate Name or Location
// SEVERITY:    High - confirmed implant persistence.
// Ref:         https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/blinder-tunnel-targets-critical-infrastructure/
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Logic: Run-key write where value name == MicrosoftRuntime OR data names RuntimeBroker.exe.
DeviceRegistryEvents
| where Timestamp > ago(7d)
| where ActionType == "RegistryValueSet"
| where RegistryKey has @"\CurrentVersion\Run"
| where RegistryValueName =~ "MicrosoftRuntime"
    or RegistryValueData has "RuntimeBroker.exe"
| project Timestamp, DeviceName, DeviceId, RegistryKey, RegistryValueName, RegistryValueData,
    InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessFolderPath, InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
    InitiatingProcessSHA1, InitiatingProcessAccountName
| order by Timestamp desc
